# Python sources at the project root — needed by the Vercel Python
# function at api/internal/welcome-send.py (instant Pulpo Pro Welcome
# dispatch). The function imports `automation.newsletter.*` + `pulpo.*`
# so those trees MUST ship to the deployment. Vercel's Python runtime
# traces explicit imports and bundles only what's reachable, so the
# heavy non-welcome modules (aesthetic_*, ai_enrichment_*, photo_quality,
# scrapers) stay out of the function bundle automatically — no
# per-module excludes needed here.
#
# Node functions (api/*.js) don't touch Python at runtime, so a few MB
# of uploaded .py files is invisible to their per-function bundles.
#
# Only the heaviest non-source artifacts stay excluded.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
fixtures/
samples/
tests/

# Local artifacts
.env
.env.local
DEPLOY.md

# Vite source (JSX) — built bundle ships from web/dist/, source isn't needed at runtime
new_ux/
docs/
nlp_keywords/
prompts/

# Node toolchain — Vercel installs from package.json itself
node_modules/